# Audi A6 C7 four-door saloon, 2011-2018.
#
# The fourth A6: the aluminium-intensive C7 body with the wider single-frame
# grille, the sharper lamps and the longer wheelbase. The Avant and allroad
# are different bodies and are not represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Audi_A6
#
# Dimensions 4.915 x 1.874 x 1.455 m, wheelbase 2.911 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a side-biased front view, not a true level
# profile; the front and rear three-quarters show the lamps and tail. The
# flank is estimated; the limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no UK chart was established. Black, silver, grey and
# blue are plain names. Weights 18, 16, 14, 12, total 60, provisional.
#
# Speed 235 km/h. Comfort 95/322, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 95. Classes 3,4.
# Dates are road presence: 2011 intro, retires staggered 2035-2038.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/audi-a6-c7.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/audi-a6-c7.dae. References:
# citycars/references/audi-a6-c7/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the rear lamps' inner join along the boot lid is not
# modelled, and there is no door-shoulder scallop or wheel-arch flare. At 128 px
# the large hexagonal grille, angular outboard lamps and rising belt read as a
# C7 A6, though it is close to the C6 from the side alone.


obj=citycar
